  "notes": "{際立|きわだ}つ is an intransitive godan verb meaning \"to stand out\" or \"to be conspicuous.\" It describes something being noticeably different or prominent compared to its surroundings.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive counterpart is {際立|きわだ}たせる (to make something stand out).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {際立|きわだ}って{美|うつく}しい (strikingly beautiful)\n- {際立|きわだ}った{特徴|とくちょう} (distinctive feature)\n- {際立|きわだ}った{存在感|そんざいかん} (striking presence)\n- {際立|きわだ}った{違|ちが}い (notable difference)\n\nUSAGE PATTERNS:\n- Often used with ている to describe a current state: {際立|きわだ}っている (stands out)\n- The past participle {際立|きわだ}った is commonly used as an adjective\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {目立|めだ}つ: More common, general \"to stand out\"\n- {際立|きわだ}つ: More literary, emphasizes contrast with surroundings\n\nREGISTER: Neutral to slightly literary.",
